(A) the rate-p good model is not the population minimiser on all of (2^-m, c_hi]
    instance d=100, m=20, p=2^-10, H(p)=0.011174; programs: true parity + rate q, only the rate code differs
    code 1 (tcommon RC code), window (2^-20, c_hi = 8.0618e-03] (kappa = 0):
        c in [9.5367e-07, 4.3294e-04]: minimiser q = 1/2^10  <- rate p (the good model)
        c in [4.3314e-04, 1.8464e-03]: minimiser q = 1/2^9
        c in [1.8472e-03, 3.7753e-03]: minimiser q = 1/2^8
        c in [3.7770e-03, 8.0618e-03]: minimiser q = 1/2^6
    code 1 (tcommon RC code), window (2^-20, c_hi = 3.6590e-03] (kappa = 30):
        c in [9.5367e-07, 4.3288e-04]: minimiser q = 1/2^10  <- rate p (the good model)
        c in [4.3306e-04, 1.8461e-03]: minimiser q = 1/2^9
        c in [1.8468e-03, 3.6590e-03]: minimiser q = 1/2^8
    code 2 (2 log r for q = 2^-r), window (2^-20, c_hi = 8.0618e-03] (kappa = 0):
        c in [9.5367e-07, 1.4237e-03]: minimiser q = 2^-10  <- rate p (the good model)
        c in [1.4244e-03, 5.4327e-03]: minimiser q = 2^-9
        c in [5.4352e-03, 8.0618e-03]: minimiser q = 2^-8
    code 2 (2 log r for q = 2^-r), window (2^-20, c_hi = 3.6590e-03] (kappa = 30):
        c in [9.5367e-07, 1.4241e-03]: minimiser q = 2^-10  <- rate p (the good model)
        c in [1.4247e-03, 3.6590e-03]: minimiser q = 2^-9
    KL(p || 2^-9) = 0.000433 bits; code 1 saves 1 bit(s) for 2^-9 against 2^-10, so 2^-9 wins for c > 4.3301e-04
    code 2 saves 0.3040 bits, so 2^-9 wins for c > 1.4243e-03
